Presidential elections were held in [[Cyprus]] on 17 February 2008, with a second round on 24 February.<ref name=Major>[http://www.iht.com/articles/ap/2008/02/17/news/Cyprus-Election.php "Incumbent eliminated from Cyprus presidential election in major surprise"] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20081215151011/http://www.iht.com/articles/ap/2008/02/17/news/Cyprus-Election.php |date=2008-12-15 }}, Associated Press (''International Herald Tribune''), 17 February 2008.</ref> The second-round winner, and thus the President of Cyprus for the next term, was [[Dimitris Christofias]].<ref>{{cite news|publisher=[[BBC]]|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/1/hi/world/europe/7261195.stm#|title=Leftist leader wins Cyprus vote|date=2008-02-24|accessdate=2008-02-24}}</ref><ref name=Results>{{cite news|publisher=Cypriot government |url=http://www.ekloges.gov.cy/index.aspx?ci=en-GB |title=Presidential Election 2008: Run-off Election: Official results |date=2008-02-24 |accessdate=2008-02-24 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20071102142751/http://www.ekloges.gov.cy/index.aspx?ci=en-GB |archivedate=2007-11-02 }}</ref>

The first round saw a close result between three leading candidates, [[Dimitris Christofias]] of [[AKEL]], [[Ioannis Kasoulidis]] of [[Democratic Rally]], and the incumbent [[Tassos Papadopoulos]]. Results showed Kasoulidis in first place with 33.51%, Christofias in second with 33.29%, and Papadopoulos in third with 31.79%. Christophias and Kasoulidis therefore participated in a second round on February 24. The elimination of Papadopoulos in the first round was viewed as surprising.<ref name=Major/>

In the second round, Christofias won with 53.37% against 46.63% for Kasoulides.<ref name=Results/> He was sworn in as President on February 28.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20080303075841/http://news.xinhuanet.com/english/2008-02/28/content_7689565.htm "New Cyprus president takes office with pledge for solution"], Xinhua (''People's Daily Online''), February 28, 2008.</ref>

According to the exit polls, Papadopoulos was voted for by 40% of "No" voters in the [[2004 Cypriot Annan Plan referendum|Annan referendum]] and 5% of the "Yes", Christofias by 35% of the "No" and 34% of the "Yes" voters and Kasoulidis by the 24% of the "No" and 62% of the "Yes" voters.<ref>{{cite news
 |publisher=[[Eleftherotypia]] 
 |url=http://www.enet.gr/online/online_text/c=110,id=75681688
 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20130217154235/http://www.enet.gr/online/online_text/c=110,id=75681688
 |url-status=dead
 |archive-date=2013-02-17
 |title=Τα πάνω-κάτω με θριαμβευτή Κασουλίδη 
 |date=2008-02-18 
 |accessdate=2008-02-19 
}}</ref>

==Candidates==
Papadopoulos ([[Democratic Party (Cyprus)|DIKO]]) announced in late July that he would run for re-election. In early July 2007, the ruling coalition (consisting of DIKO, [[Progressive Party of Working People|AKEL]] and [[Movement for Social Democracy|EDEK]]) fell apart due to a lack of consensus on a common candidate for the presidential elections; AKEL general secretary Dimitris Christofias was proposed as a common candidate by AKEL, but rejected by DIKO and EDEK (who both will support Papadopoulos' bid for reelection), which AKEL took as a reason to leave the ruling coalition. Thus, both Papadopoulos and Christophias contested the election.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://english.people.com.cn/90001/90777/6212805.html|publisher=People's Daily Online|title=Cyprus coalition government dissolved|date=2007-07-11|accessdate=2007-11-06}}</ref> The [[Ecological and Environmental Movement]] (KOP) decided on November 18, 2007 to support Papadopoulos.<ref name="eco">{{cite news|url=http://www.phileleftheros.com/main/main.asp?gid=334&id=520473|title=The ecologists decided to support the Tassos Papadopulos' candidateship|publisher=Phileleftheros|date=2007-11-18|accessdate=2007-11-18}}</ref> The movement supported him in 2003 as well.

Furthermore, the [[Democratic Rally]] support [[Member of the European Parliament|MEP]] Ioannis Kasoulidis, a former foreign minister,<ref>[http://www.iht.com/articles/ap/2007/07/11/europe/EU-POL-Cyprus-Government.php 4 ministers quit after Cyprus' ruling coalition splits - International Herald Tribune<!-- Bot generated title -->]</ref> and [[Kostas Themistokleous]], a former minister of agriculture and environment, also contested the election.

Controversial MEP [[Marios Matsakis]] announced on 29 December 2007 that he would contest the election. Marios Matsakis was elected two times as a member of the Cypriot parliament and once as member of the Εuropean Parliament with the support of DIKO.<ref>{{cite news|title=Fiery MEP to stand in Cyprus poll|publisher=ekathimerini.com|date=2007-12-29|accessdate=2007-12-30|url=http://www.ekathimerini.com/4dcgi/news/content.asp?aid=91582|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140911122545/http://www.ekathimerini.com/4dcgi/news/content.asp?aid=91582|archive-date=2014-09-11|url-status=dead}}</ref>

The Secretariat of the Movement of the [[United Democrats]] initially considered to support Themistokleous<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.simerini.com.cy/nqcontent.cfm?a_id=314751 |title=The United Democrats with Themistocleous |publisher=Simerini |date=2007-10-12 |accessdate=2007-10-30 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20071227015439/http://www.simerini.com.cy/nqcontent.cfm?a_id=314751 |archivedate=2007-12-27 }}</ref> but at the end they supported Christophias to minimize the possibility of Papadopoulos' re-election.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.politis-news.com/cgibin/hweb?-A=747151&-V=archivearticles|publisher=Politis Online|title=The United Democrats votes sensibly|date=2007-10-15|accessdate=2007-10-30|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071227043502/http://www.politis-news.com/cgibin/hweb?-A=747151&-V=archivearticles|archive-date=2007-12-27|url-status=dead}}</ref>

Nine candidates were eventually approved to participate in the elections. Each candidate had to be recommended by one Cypriot citizen and supported by eight more.

The names of the candidates announced on 18 January 2008<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.simerini.com.cy/nqcontent.cfm?a_id=325541 |publisher=Simerini |title=Μάχη εντυπώσεων στην υποβολή υποψηφιοτήτων |date=2008-01-19 |accessdate=2009-01-19 }}{{dead link|date=December 2016 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> were:
*[[Tassos Papadopoulos]], supported by DIKO, EDEK,<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.politis.com.cy/cgibin/hweb?-A=742249&-V=archivearticles&-p |publisher=Politis Online |title=EDEK's bet |date=2007-09-24 |accessdate=2007-10-30 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20110718163540/http://www.politis.com.cy/cgibin/hweb?-A=742249&-V=archivearticles&-p |archivedate=2011-07-18 }}</ref> [[European Party (Cyprus)|Evroko]],<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.evropaikokomma.org/MAIN/default.aspx?ItemID=263&mid=119&tabid=1 |title=The European Party supports Tassos Papadopoulos |publisher=Press release of European Party |accessdate=2007-10-02 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20071227072229/http://www.evropaikokomma.org/MAIN/default.aspx?ItemID=263&mid=119&tabid=1 |archivedate=2007-12-27 }}</ref> [[Fighting Democratic Movement|ADIK]],<ref>{{cite news|publisher=Radio Pafos 93.7 FM|url=http://www.radiopafos.com/index.php?categoryid=18&p2_articleid=1096|title=ADIK supports Tassos Papadopoulos as well|date=2007-10-11|accessdate=2007-10-30}}</ref> KOP<ref name="eco" />
*[[Dimitris Christofias]], supported by [[Progressive Party of Working People|AKEL]], [[United Democrats]]<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.simerini.com.cy/nqcontent.cfm?a_id=315066 |publisher=Simireni |title=The United Democrats "vote" Christophias |date=2007-10-15 |accessdate=2007-10-30 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20071227015445/http://www.simerini.com.cy/nqcontent.cfm?a_id=315066 |archivedate=2007-12-27 }}</ref>
*[[Ioannis Kasoulidis]], supported by [[Democratic Rally|DISY]], Kinima Eleftheron Politon,<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.phileleftheros.com/main/main.asp?gid=488&id=523988&issuenum=17254|title=Ο Κασουλίδης προσφέρει διεξόδους απεγκλωβισμού|publisher=Phileleftheros|date=2007-12-07|accessdate=2008-01-02}}</ref> Evropaiki Dimokratia,<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.maxinewspaper.com/index.php?news=8909 |title=H Ευρωπαϊκή Δημοκρατία σε ανακοίνωσή της αναφέρει ότι η υποψηφιότητα Kασουλίδη προχωρά με προτάσεις για τα προβλήματα της χώρας |date=2007-10-23 |accessdate=2008-01-02 |publisher=Η Μάχη |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160121053138/http://www.maxinewspaper.com/index.php?news=8909 |archivedate=2016-01-21 }}</ref> Laiko Sosialistiko Kinima
