==Campaign==
===Second round===
After the first round of the election and the elimination of Papadopoulos, the latter's party, [[DIKO]], announced its support for Christofias<ref name=Edge>[http://www.news.com.au/story/0,23599,23250278-1702,00.html "Communist chief gains edge in Cyprus poll"]  {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090116104510/http://www.news.com.au/story/0%2C23599%2C23250278-1702%2C00.html |date=January 16, 2009 }}, AFP (news.com.au), February 21, 2008.</ref> although Papadopoulos himself stayed neutral.{{Citation needed|date=February 2008}} Christofias had offered three ministerial positions to DIKO, including that of Minister of Foreign Affairs, in addition to the post of President of the House of Representatives, while Kasoulides had offered five ministerial positions in exchange for DIKO's support.<ref name=Edge/> [[EDEK]] also backed Christofias, on the proposal of its Political Bureau, with 109 members of its Central Committee voting in favor of supporting Christofias, five voting against, and two abstaining.<ref>[http://www.financialmirror.com/more_news.php?id=10059&nt=Politics "Cyprus Socialists supports Christofia’s candidacy"]{{Dead link|date=October 2018 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}, ''Financial Mirror'', February 21, 2008.</ref> The [[Cypriot Orthodox Church]] leader [[Archbishop Chrysostomos II]] backed Kasoulidis.<ref name=Edge/>

[[Ecological and Environmental Movement]] on 21 February 2008 decided to support Dimitris Christofias.

Evroko, [[ADIK]] and Marios Matsakis announced that they will support neither of the two candidates.

Kostas Themistokleous backed Ioannis Kasoulidis.

==Debates==
On 26 January 2008 the three main candidates, Papadopoulos, Christofias, and Kasoulidis, debated on television. The debate was transmitted by all Cypriot TV stations.<ref>{{cite news|publisher=Politis |url=http://www.politis.com.cy/cgibin/hweb?-A=769792&-V=articles&-p |title=Παράθυρο ευκαιρίας |date=2008-01-25 |accessdate=2008-01-25 |author=Katerina Zorba |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20110718163719/http://www.politis.com.cy/cgibin/hweb?-A=769792&-V=articles&-p |archivedate=2011-07-18 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news|publisher=Simerini |url=http://www.simerini.com.cy/nqcontent.cfm?a_id=326472 |title=Everyone declares himself as a winner |date=2008-01-25 |accessdate=2008-01-25 |author=Marios Manousopoulos }}{{dead link|date=December 2016 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> The three candidates were questioned by journalists from  [[Cyprus Broadcasting Corporation|RIK]], MEGA, [[ANT1 Cyprus|ANT1]], [[Sigma TV]] and [[CNC Plus TV]]. The debate started at 9.45PM local time and lasted 1 hour and 50 minutes. Each candidate had three minutes to answer each question and 1.5 minute for every follow-up question. The procedure was divided in 6 sections and, at the end of each section, each candidate had 3 minutes to give a short speech and 1.5 minute for a short comment.<ref>{{cite news|publisher=iKypros.com|url=http://www.ikypros.com/cgibin/hweb?-A=33085&-V=ikypros&w=|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110613145650/http://www.ikypros.com/cgibin/hweb?-A=33085&-V=ikypros&w=|url-status=dead|archive-date=2011-06-13|title=Τρεις υποψήφιοι προέδροι στην πρώτη αναμέτρηση|date=2008-01-24|accessdate=2008-01-26}}</ref>

On 14 February, a second debate was held. The subject of discussion was the [[Cyprus dispute]].<ref>{{cite news|publisher=Politis |url=http://www.politis.com.cy/cgibin/hweb?-A=774323&-V=articles |title=Ντιμπέιτ για τα λάθη και λίγα για το μέλλον |date=2008-02-14 |accessdate=2008-02-15 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20110718163733/http://www.politis.com.cy/cgibin/hweb?-A=774323&-V=articles |archivedate=2011-07-18 }}</ref>

